  "source": "eval.loader.sample(claims, seed=42) - the 2026-08-19 re-baseline",
  "why": "PR #75 regenerated the corpus to derive counterparty_exists from damage_type. Removing one random.random() call shifted the generator's stream, so every gt_id survived and the claim behind it did not: policy_no moved on 957 of 1000 records, damage_description on 945, content_type on 176. Re-pinned rather than patched, for the same reason as the 2026-08-04 re-baseline - loosening the guard to fit the drift would defeat the guard.",
  "pool": "content_type == 'claim' only, 903 of 1000. Extraction never sees the other two types: classification exits early for them (design doc §4), and their only filled field is policy_no, so scoring them would raise the number without the model having done anything.",
